build/
build_3ds/
# any other out-of-tree build dir (build-ubsan/ once had a 4.9 MB binary committed)
build-*/
*.3dsx
*.elf
*.smdh
*.cia
*.map
*.shbin
.DS_Store
*.o
*.a
*.so
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
# CMake-generated Makefiles/scripts only ever land inside a build dir (already
# ignored above). The top-level Makefile and t2k_3ds/Makefile are SOURCE.
build*/**/Makefile
build*/**/*.cmake
docs/validation/*.wav

# data/music/ and music/: the DESKTOP runtime soundtrack folder (music_sdl.cpp
# resolveMusicDir -- CWD-first, same lookup order as levels.json), populated
# locally from soundtracks/dsp/ so a dev machine's build plays the same DSP
# soundtrack the 3DS SD card does. Same "never commit copyrighted audio" rule
# as the soundtracks/ block below -- this is a LOCAL staging copy, not source.
# (The desktop is run from the repo root, so the staging copy stays at
# /data/music even though the tracked level data moved to t2k_core/data/.)
data/music/
/music/

# Soundtracks: version the pipeline scripts + folder structure only. Never
# commit the audio (huge + copyrighted) or the big generated fingerprint data.
soundtracks/**/*.flac
soundtracks/**/*.wav
soundtracks/**/*.mp3
soundtracks/**/*.ogg
soundtracks/**/*.mod
soundtracks/**/*.dsp
soundtracks/catalog.json
soundtracks/unique.json

# ...except the Tempest 2000 MOD album SOURCES under soundtracks/mod/. These
# stream natively (never re-encoded), have circulated publicly on GitHub for
# years, and ship with the code so a clone can build a complete CIA without
# fetching anything. The deployable copies under soundtracks/dsp/ stay ignored:
# they are generated by the pipeline, not authored.
!soundtracks/mod/*.mod

# Built binaries from the vendored toolchain pieces (tools/build_dspadpcm.sh).
tools/bin/

# The project-local python env ./build.sh bootstrap creates when the ambient
# interpreter lacks curl_cffi/beautifulsoup4/pyflakes. Recreated on demand;
# never a source.
.venv/

# Third-party SFX + the editing projects built from them are TRACKED so the
# repo clones and builds exactly as envisioned (see NOTICE.txt: these assets
# are NOT covered by the MIT grant and carry their own copyright).
# Binaries: compiled + reference executables/assets (build outputs are above).
# Source, docs and validation images stay tracked.
*.exe
*.dll
*.bin
*.lib
*.dylib
*.pdb
*.obj
*.ico
*.res
.sfx_preview/
# Audacity write-ahead logs are transient working state (the .aup3 single-file DB
# is the source of truth) -- never commit them, anywhere.
*.aup3-wal
# Authoring scratch dropped at the repo ROOT stays out of history. The KEPT
# authoring sources (source WAVs + Audacity projects) live under
# t2k_core/assets/sfx/sources/ and ARE tracked; these root-anchored patterns only
# catch stray copies left at the top level.
/aww.wav
/*.aup3
/t2k_pickup.aup3
/freesound_*.mp3

# Reference-only trees consulted for reverse-engineering. NEVER commit these:
# tempest2k/ is LEAKED proprietary Tempest 2000 source (its own headers say so,
# and that it builds byte-identical to the retail 1994 game). It is read here for
# BEHAVIOURAL facts only -- mechanisms, timings -- never for geometry or artwork.
# Committing it would put third-party source in this repo's history permanently.
tempest2k/
# t2k_dos/ is the same leaked Tempest 2000 source family -- the DOS/PC port
# (TASM x86: TEMPEST.ASM, VECTORS.ASM, WEBS.ASM, 3D.ASM ...), comments blanked
# the same way tempest2k/'s are. Read for BEHAVIOURAL facts only (the camera
# law, timings, mechanisms) -- never geometry, artwork or verbatim code.
t2k_dos/
# Same leaked DOS source family, but landed under names the `t2k_dos/` pattern
# above does NOT catch: the archive and its extracted folder (3D.ASM, AUDIO.ASM,
# BONUS1UP.ASM ...). Same rule -- behavioural facts only, never commit.
Tempest2000_dos/
Tempest 2000 (DOS, Source code).7z
# ...and a loose copy of one of its translation units read at the repo root
# (TEMPEST.ASM was dropped here on 2026-09-02 to recover the powerup message
# strings). Same rule: never commit it.
TEMPEST.asm
TEMPEST.ASM
# NOTE: `soundtracks/` used to be ignored wholesale here. That is removed: the
# pipeline scripts, the pinned `track_map.json`, and the MOD album sources under
# `soundtracks/mod/` are tracked, and the audio itself is excluded by the
# extension rules in the soundtracks block above. A directory-level ignore also
# makes every new file under it silently untrackable, which is how `track_map.json`
# nearly got lost.

# typhoon_extract/: the *.json under this tree (webs/, enemies/) are our own
# derived extraction (legitimate RE work product, tracked normally). The raw
# game binary itself -- packed and unpacked -- is not; never commit Typhoon
# 2001's copyrighted executable/asset blob into this repo's history.
typhoon_extract/typhoon.packed
typhoon_extract/typhoon.unpacked

# visual-validator drive frames/logs occasionally land in the repo ROOT rather
# than the scratchpad. Evidence worth keeping belongs in docs/validation/.
scratchpad_*

# FUSE silly-rename leftovers: the Mandarine AppImage keeps deleted files open,
# so unlinked zero-link-count stubs survive until the mount releases them.
.fuse_hidden*

# Python bytecode from the Python reference port. 36 of these were
# tracked, so every run of the reference implementation dirtied the working
# tree and showed up in diffs.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Tempest 3000 (Nuon): the disc image and anything extracted out of it that is
# the game's own code/data are copyrighted -- never commit them. Same rule the
# typhoon_extract/ block above applies: our DERIVED geometry JSON under
# t3k_extract/ is tracked, the binaries and RAM dumps are not.
Tempest 3000*.iso
t3k_extract/nuon.run
t3k_extract/nuon.n16
t3k_extract/*.bin

# The CIA packaging tools (makerom, bannertool) that get_cia_tools.sh
# builds on demand -- neither ships with devkitPro.
t2k_3ds/tools/.ciatools/

# Runner runtime state (recreated per run; never commit)
tools/runner/state.json
tools/runner/runner.lock
tools/runner/logs/
tools/runner/__pycache__/

# NFS silly-rename artifacts. When a file is unlinked while another process
# still holds it open, NFS renames it to .nfsXXXX rather than deleting it, and
# it lingers until that handle closes. It is never ours to commit -- and it
# would otherwise block tools/build_production.sh, which correctly refuses to
# build from a dirty tree.
.nfs*

# Local-only working material. These stay on disk for whoever is working in this
# checkout and never enter the repo: the notes tree, the editor's tooling
# directory, and the local automation scripts.
/docs/
/.kilo/

# The agent contract ships: it is the enforceable ARM11/VFP ruleset that every
# PR is cut against, together with the gate scripts and contract corpus it names.
# The rest of tools/runner/ (scheduler, worker, live state, logs) stays local.
# Every script tools/check.sh invokes MUST be negated here: a gate that is
# gitignored is a gate that silently disappears on a fresh clone, which is the
# exact "verification decayed" defect class check.sh exists to prevent.
/tools/runner/*
!/tools/runner/gates_vfp.py
!/tools/runner/audit_arm11_math.py
!/tools/runner/audit_r11_idiv.py
!/tools/runner/audit_c_with_classes.py
!/tools/runner/contracts/
